    "Anthropic first-party list prices. Tiers: input, output, cache_write_5m, cache_write_1h, cache_read.",
    "Keys match the response `model` field by substring (family-version or version-family); longer keys win, so opus-5.5 is picked over opus-5.",
    "Each model holds a list of rates. A rate applies from its effective_from date (YYYY-MM-DD, local time) until the next one; a rate with no effective_from applies from the beginning. Add a new entry to schedule a price change instead of editing the old one.",
    "Opus 4.5 and newer are $5/$25 (Opus 5.5: $4/$20); only Opus 4.0/4.1 and Opus 3 carry $15/$75.",
    "Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1 read cache at 0.025x input ($0.25/MTok) and Opus 5.5 at 0.05x ($0.20/MTok), not the usual 0.1x."
